# Netlify headers — https://docs.netlify.com/routing/headers/
#
# Note on the split below: the CSS and JS are cached for a year because they
# carry a ?v= cache-buster in index.html, which makes every edit a brand-new
# URL. The images are deliberately NOT given the same treatment — they have no
# version query, so if you ever swap profile.jpg for a new photo the URL is
# identical and a one-year cache would keep serving the old one for a year.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

# The HTML is the only file that must never be stale: it is what points at
# the current ?v= values, so a cached copy would pin the site to old assets.
# no-cache still allows a 304 (a few bytes) when nothing changed.
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/pictures/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
